# BusGo conventions

`tsconfig.json` has `strict: true`. Keep it on. Do not use `any`, non-null assertions, or unchecked casts to silence the compiler.

## React

Use function components. Style only with Tailwind `className`. Do not add CSS modules, styled-components, or inline `style` objects.

```tsx
export function SeatButton({ label }: { label: string }) {
  return (
    <button type="button" className="rounded-lg bg-brand px-4 py-2 font-bold text-white">
      {label}
    </button>
  );
}
```

## API routes

Put route handlers under `src/app/api/`. Validate JSON bodies with Zod before using them. Return `Response.json` with an explicit status.

```ts
import { z } from "zod";

const bodySchema = z.object({
  busId: z.string().min(1),
  seatIds: z.array(z.string().min(1)).min(1),
});

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const parsed = bodySchema.safeParse(await request.json());
  if (!parsed.success) {
    return Response.json({ error: "Invalid booking." }, { status: 400 });
  }
  return Response.json({ busId: parsed.data.busId });
}
```

## Database

Import the shared client from `@/prisma/db` (`src/prisma/db.ts`). Do not construct a new Prisma client in routes, pages, or scripts.

```ts
import { db } from "@/prisma/db";

const bus = await db.orm.public.Bus.first({ id });
```
